# Build context hygiene. Without this file every `docker build` uploads the
# whole working tree - including a ~500MB node_modules, the .git history, and
# the client's PDFs under context/ - before the first instruction runs.
#
# Nothing here may exclude package.json, package-lock.json, or a workspace
# manifest: the Dockerfiles copy those first and `npm ci` cannot run without
# them.

# Dependencies - reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile. Copying the
# host's tree in would also drag in platform-specific binaries built for
# Windows.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs - regenerated in the builder stage.
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
build
out
*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control and CI metadata
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Secrets. .env is gitignored but may exist locally, and a build context is not
# a private place: anything here lands in an image layer (CLAUDE.md §8).
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Client material and project documentation - not needed to run the app, and
# context/ holds the signed agreement and meeting reports.
context
*.md
!README.md

# Local tooling and agent state
.claude
.claude-flow
.swarm
.agents
.vscode
.idea

# Test and coverage artifacts
coverage
.nyc_output

# Container definitions themselves
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
